# A constant naming itself as a map value. The cell completes and the map
# holds itself, so rendering walks a ring, and the guard that stops the walk
# keys on the cell rather than only on the records around it.
#
# The map appears twice because the cell is what repeats: the walk reaches
# it, prints what it holds, and finds the same cell inside. A record knot
# shows its type once for the same reason — there the record is the
# repeating identity.
ring = { "a":ring }

pub play = print "{ring}"
